--- Technical ---
### Changed

- Integrate the M9 frontend redesign branches into `main` and add the v1.9.0 release notes at a single point for tagging. ([#244](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/244))

### Added

- Add inline citation badges to sanitized assistant Markdown, with numbered badges, hover and focus tooltips, and unanchored citations retained in the sources list. ([#245](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/245))
- Add actionable suggested steps as primary ticket-header controls, with remaining steps in an overflow menu and existing generic controls available as fallback. ([#237](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/237))
- Add a keyboard-operable command palette across all pages, opened with `Ctrl/Cmd+K`, with navigation from `NavRegistry` and debounced, cancellable ticket search. ([#236](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/236))
- Add optimistic status updates to the board and ticket detail view, reconciling successful changes and restoring prior state when a transition is rejected. ([#235](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/235))
- Replace ticket status and assignee dialogs with inline `MudMenu` popovers that apply changes through the existing command handlers. ([#234](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/234))
- Add inline citation badges with keyboard-accessible tooltips in assistant answers, retaining a numbered sources list for citations that are not anchored. ([#233](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/233))
- Add the active agent roster to each chat system prompt and instruct the assistant to use only listed names when assigning tickets. ([#221](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/221))
- Force `check_grounding` through `tool_choice` once after retrieval when no grounding check has run, so the verdict is computed before the first streamed token. ([#218](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/218))
- Add design tokens for palette, spacing, radius, elevation, and semantic chip colors, and use them across the stylesheets and `AppTheme`. Replace `KpiCard.Accent` with the `KpiAccent` enum. ([#213](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/213))

### Fixed

- Fix board card title clamping by wrapping the title link so its two-line ellipsis applies without grid-item blockification. ([#240](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/240))
- Fix the assistant composer layout by applying the panel styles through `::deep .assistant-chat`, keeping the send button inside the panel. ([#239](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/239))
- Fix the ticket queue's `Category` column by setting its width to `140px` and rendering its header with the uppercase `tickets-table__label` class. ([#238](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/238))
- Add system-prompt rules requiring successful tool results before claiming a change was made and avoiding unnecessary confirmation when the user has already requested a change. ([#223](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/223))
- Render ticket summary timestamps in the configured `Anthropic:UserTimeZone` before including them in the model prompt. ([#222](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/222))
- Fix knowledge-base search failures by returning technical exceptions as errors while keeping the unavailable path distinct and transient faults rethrown. ([#220](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/220))
- Replace lexical grounding as the primary evaluator with semantic sentence-to-passage similarity, retaining `LexicalGroundingEvaluator` as a fallback. ([#219](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/219))
